THE PACIFIC COAST TITLE INSURANCE COMPANY
Title Insurance Policy

This policy is issued by The Pacific Coast Title Insurance Company, hereinafter "the Company," to the insured, hereinafter "the Insured," for the property described herein.

I. INSURANCE COVERAGE

The Company insures the Insured against loss or damage, not to exceed the amount of insurance stated in the Declarations, resulting from:

A. Any defect in or lien or encumbrance on the title to the estate or interest described in the Declarations;

B. Unmarketability of the title;

C. Any claim that is first made and reported to the Company during the policy term and that arises out of:

1. Any defect in or lien or encumbrance on the title;
2. The invalidity or unenforceability of any lien or encumbrance resulting from any fraud, forgery, or duress;
3. The invalidity or unenforceability of any lien or encumbrance that is a result of any mechanic's, materialman's, or laborer's lien, or any other lien or encumbrance that is created by the Insured's actions;
4. Any final court order or judgment that is adverse to the Insured's title or interest in the property;
5. The existence of any easement, or any right of way, that is not excepted in the policy and that interferes with the use or enjoyment of the property;
6. Any misdescription of the property in the policy or in any prior policy or policy endorsement;
7. Any right of a third party to physical occupation of the property that is adverse to the Insured's title or interest in the property;
8. Any claim that is based on a violation of any restrictive covenant that runs with the land, except for any restrictive covenant that is contained in the policy or in any prior policy or policy endorsement;
9. Any claim that is based on a violation of any building or zoning law, except for any violation that is contained in the policy or in any prior policy or policy endorsement;
